============================================================
PARITY NOTES
============================================================
- Pure-presentational parity decision (matches the InlineCallout 0124 / Delta 0081 /
  MetricCard 0095 precedent): the web <StatusHero> has no fetch/cache/promise, so it
  has NO loading/error/stale/offline branch. Reproducing only the source's REAL
  branches (5 status tiers x headline-override x subline x subline-gated live x CTA)
  is faithful; fabricating fetch states would invent UI the source does not have.
- Tokens (P1/S9): healthy->success, degraded->warning, unhealthy->danger,
  unknown->neutral, maintenance->info (TSTone -> theme-aware Color.TS.*); no raw hex.
- i18n (P1/S10): 6 keys owned (statusHero.headline.{5 tiers} + statusHero.live),
  fallbacks byte-identical to STATUS_CONFIG.defaultHeadline + the web "Live" word.
- Shared components mapped: GlassPanel->TSGlassPanel(+glow), Button->TSButton,
  LiveIndicator->LiveIndicator(variant:.dot) (0094). Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened
  with slug "StatusHero". A11y: decorative glyph hidden, status region spoken as one
  updatesFrequently element, CTA its own labelled button, adaptive size-class layout.

